-> Type intersection: value must match ALL types in the intersection
Point = Particle ∩ { _class ∈ "Point", x ∈ Number, y ∈ Number }
p = Point { x = 1, y = 2 }

-> A Point is both a Point and an Object
assert p ∈ Point ∩ Object

-> A number is a Number (trivial intersection with itself)
n = 42
assert n ∈ Number ∩ Number

-> Intersection with union: ∩ binds tighter than ∪
-> `Number ∩ Number ∪ String` means `(Number ∩ Number) ∪ String`
assert n ∈ Number ∩ Number ∪ String
s = "hello"
assert s ∈ Number ∩ Number ∪ String

-> Negated intersection check
assert s ∉ Number ∩ Number
assert n ∉ String ∩ String
